{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PsgdMDnDCoCzQAnRt6QSYD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Corpus 01 — Product Launch\n2\t\n3\t**Stresses:** hero moments · low information density · brand personality · visual impact\n4\t**Target length:** 10–12 slides\n5\t**Audience:** press and prospective customers at a launch event, projected on a large screen\n6\t**Failure modes this corpus exposes:** generic template look, timid color, wall-of-bullets on slides that should carry one idea, no typographic hierarchy\n7\t\n8\t> All content below is fictional. \"Meridian\" is an invented company used solely as\n9\t> neutral test material — any resemblance to a real product is coincidental.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## Brief\n14\t\n15\tMeridian is launching **Meridian Field**, an offline-first data collection tool for\n16\tenvironmental survey teams. Today's event announces general availability and pricing.\n17\tThe deck is speaker-led: the presenter talks, the slides punctuate.\n18\t\n19\t**Tone:** confident, plainspoken, a little bit outdoorsy. Not a SaaS-blue enterprise deck.\n20\t\n21\t---\n22\t\n23\t## Content\n24\t\n25\t### Opening\n26\t\n27\t**Meridian Field**\n28\tSurvey anywhere. Sync when you can.\n29\t\n30\t### The problem\n31\t\n32\tEnvironmental survey teams work where connectivity does not.\n33\t\n34\tField biologists, hydrologists and air-quality technicians spend their days in\n35\tcanyons, wetlands and basements. The tools they are given assume a live connection.\n36\tSo the work happens twice: once on paper in the field, once again at a desk that\n37\tnight — transcription that costs the average team **6 hours per field day** and\n38\tintroduces errors nobody catches until the dataset is already in a report.\n39\t\n40\t### The stat that matters\n41\t\n42\t**41%** of survey datasets contain at least one transcription error traceable to\n43\tmanual re-entry.\n44\t\n45\t*Source: fictional internal study, 2026. Placeholder figure for layout purposes.*\n46\t\n47\t### What we built\n48\t\n49\tMeridian Field is a full survey client that runs entirely offline.\n50\t\n51\t- Complete data capture with no network dependency at any point\n52\t- Conflict-aware sync that merges edits from multiple surveyors on reconnect\n53\t- Photo, audio and GPS capture attached to every record\n54\t- Schema validation at entry time, not after upload\n55\t\n56\t### How it works\n57\t\n58\tThree steps:\n59\t\n60\t1. **Define** your survey schema once, on the web. Field types, validation rules,\n61\t   required photos.\n62\t2. **Collect** on any device, offline, for as long as the fieldwork takes. Days or weeks.\n63\t3. **Sync** when you reach connectivity. Conflicts surface as a review queue, never\n64\t   as silent overwrites.\n65\t\n66\t### Proof\n67\t\n68\tCascade Watershed Alliance ran Meridian Field across a 14-week stream survey with\n69\tnine simultaneous surveyors.\n70\t\n71\t- **0** records lost\n72\t- **6.5 hrs** saved per field day\n73\t- **14 weeks** of continuous offline operation before first sync\n74\t\n75\t> \"We stopped doing the evening data-entry shift entirely. That is the whole review.\"\n76\t> — Field Operations Lead, Cascade Watershed Alliance *(fictional quote)*\n77\t\n78\t### Pricing\n79\t\n80\tThree tiers, priced per active surveyor per month:\n81\t\n82\t| Tier | Price | For |\n83\t|---|---|---|\n84\t| **Solo** | $19 | Independent consultants and single-surveyor projects |\n85\t| **Team** | $49 | Multi-surveyor projects with shared schemas and sync review |\n86\t| **Institution** | Custom | Agencies and universities needing SSO, audit logs and data residency |\n87\t\n88\tAll tiers include unlimited offline duration and unlimited photo capture.\n89\t\n90\t### Availability\n91\t\n92\tGenerally available today on iOS, Android and Windows tablets.\n93\tFree for the first 30 days, no card required.\n94\t\n95\t### Closing\n96\t\n97\t**Survey anywhere. Sync when you can.**\n98\tmeridian.example/field\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"170e2903-4018-4657-846f-4d4287473de7","uuid":"c9cad926-bfdf-4042-b0be-727de8bd3274","timestamp":"2026-07-28T10:29:25.215Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/brycewang/Documents/GitHub/many-ppt-skills/benchmark/results/run-01/frontend-slides/01-product-launch/rep-01/workspace/input.md","content":"# Corpus 01 — Product Launch\n\n**Stresses:** hero moments · low information density · brand personality · visual impact\n**Target length:** 10–12 slides\n**Audience:** press and prospective customers at a launch event, projected on a large screen\n**Failure modes this corpus exposes:** generic template look, timid color, wall-of-bullets on slides that should carry one idea, no typographic hierarchy\n\n> All content below is fictional. \"Meridian\" is an invented company used solely as\n> neutral test material — any resemblance to a real product is coincidental.\n\n---\n\n## Brief\n\nMeridian is launching **Meridian Field**, an offline-first data collection tool for\nenvironmental survey teams. Today's event announces general availability and pricing.\nThe deck is speaker-led: the presenter talks, the slides punctuate.\n\n**Tone:** confident, plainspoken, a little bit outdoorsy. Not a SaaS-blue enterprise deck.\n\n---\n\n## Content\n\n### Opening\n\n**Meridian Field**\nSurvey anywhere. Sync when you can.\n\n### The problem\n\nEnvironmental survey teams work where connectivity does not.\n\nField biologists, hydrologists and air-quality technicians spend their days in\ncanyons, wetlands and basements. The tools they are given assume a live connection.\nSo the work happens twice: once on paper in the field, once again at a desk that\nnight — transcription that costs the average team **6 hours per field day** and\nintroduces errors nobody catches until the dataset is already in a report.\n\n### The stat that matters\n\n**41%** of survey datasets contain at least one transcription error traceable to\nmanual re-entry.\n\n*Source: fictional internal study, 2026. Placeholder figure for layout purposes.*\n\n### What we built\n\nMeridian Field is a full survey client that runs entirely offline.\n\n- Complete data capture with no network dependency at any point\n- Conflict-aware sync that merges edits from multiple surveyors on reconnect\n- Photo, audio and GPS capture attached to every record\n- Schema validation at entry time, not after upload\n\n### How it works\n\nThree steps:\n\n1. **Define** your survey schema once, on the web. Field types, validation rules,\n   required photos.\n2. **Collect** on any device, offline, for as long as the fieldwork takes. Days or weeks.\n3. **Sync** when you reach connectivity. Conflicts surface as a review queue, never\n   as silent overwrites.\n\n### Proof\n\nCascade Watershed Alliance ran Meridian Field across a 14-week stream survey with\nnine simultaneous surveyors.\n\n- **0** records lost\n- **6.5 hrs** saved per field day\n- **14 weeks** of continuous offline operation before first sync\n\n> \"We stopped doing the evening data-entry shift entirely. That is the whole review.\"\n> — Field Operations Lead, Cascade Watershed Alliance *(fictional quote)*\n\n### Pricing\n\nThree tiers, priced per active surveyor per month:\n\n| Tier | Price | For |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Solo** | $19 | Independent consultants and single-surveyor projects |\n| **Team** | $49 | Multi-surveyor projects with shared schemas and sync review |\n| **Institution** | Custom | Agencies and universities needing SSO, audit logs and data residency |\n\nAll tiers include unlimited offline duration and unlimited photo capture.\n\n### Availability\n\nGenerally available today on iOS, Android and Windows tablets.\nFree for the first 30 days, no card required.\n\n### Closing\n\n**Survey anywhere. Sync when you can.**\nmeridian.example/field\n","numLines":99,"startLine":1,"totalLines":99}}}
